{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>For every matter.</b> The Sage knows that for every matter there is a set time, and he does not enter into conflict with a man whose hour is playing in his favor. The meaning of \"for the evil of man\": even though he knows that there is a time for every matter, he does not know when the time will arrive — and this is a great evil."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:28:22.867951161Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}